0 @N4287@ NOTE === Resumen de la vida de la persona ===
1 CONT Peter of Aragon (Catalan: Pere d'Aragó, Spanish: Pedro de Aragón; 1305 – 4 November 1381) was an infante (royal prince) of the Crown of Aragon who served three successive kings as a soldier, diplomat and counsellor before joining the Franciscan
1 CONC s in 1358.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Peter was the Count of Ribagorza (1322–1358), Count of Empúries (1325–1341) and Count of Prades (1341–1358). He was the most important counsellor of Alfonso IV and Peter IV, and was regent during the absence of the latter (1354–1356). He t
1 CONC ook part in most of the major military conflicts of their reigns down to his death.
1 CONT Peter was also an author and patron of letters. As a Franciscan, he advocated an end to the Avignon Papacy and wrote a prophetic tract to that effect.
1 CONT 
1 CONT By his marriage to Joan, Peter had four children:
1 CONT - Alfonso, who inherited Ribagorza and later became duke of Gandia[2]
1 CONT - John, who inherited Prades, Entença and the seneschalcy of Catalonia and was a candidate for the Aragonese crown before the Compromise of Caspe[17]
1 CONT - James, who became a bishop of Tortosa (1362–1369), bishop of Valencia (1369–1396) and later a cardinal[2]
1 CONT - Eleanor, who married King Peter I of Cyprus
