0 @N13920@ NOTE === Can Vinyals ===
1 CONT Can Vinyals is a noble and stately manor house located on the outskirts of the town, just over a kilometer from the old town and right next to the road that goes to Sant Llorenç de les Arenes. This house has different very clear construction stage
1 CONC s, the most significant of which is a large circular tower built at the end of the nineteenth century reminiscent of the towers of Peralada Castle.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The interior of the house was restored by Bonaventura de Vinyals who was advised by the modernist architect Rafel Masó i Valentí, the promoter of the luxurious urbanization of s'Agaró in Platja d'Aro. In the center of the house, on the ground fl
1 CONC oor there is a chapel dedicated to the Virgin of Carmen, built in 1718 by Josep de Vinyals and which Botet i Sisó describes as a public chapel.
1 CONT 
1 CONT At the door of the chapel you can read the following inscription:"EDO D·LGENTES MEDI/GO ET QUI MANE VI·GLANT AD MEINVENEN PROV 8 JOSPHEI VINYAS VEGUER ME FIERT FESIT DIE 20 MAY 1718" which would come to say: "I love those who love me and those wh
1 CONC o get up early to look for me will find me. Book of Proverbs, 8. Josep Vinyals Veguer made me do it. May 20, 1718." The Vinyals family was one of the noblest in the area, receiving a privilege from the nobility of Charles V, which gave rise to th
1 CONC e saying of "the girls of can Vinyals ennoble the pairals".
1 CONT 
1 CONT Source:
1 CONT http://www.flaca.cat/coneix/llocs-dinteres/can-vinyals/
0 @N13921@ NOTE === José de Vinyals y de Veguer ===
1 CONT Bernardo Vinyals, native of Flassá and resident of Foixá (Girona), He was also graced with the same privilege for all his offspring. male and female by Don Carlos I, given in Barcelona, on June 23, 1555. His descendant Pedro de Vinyals y Veguer
1 CONC , supporter of the Archduke-pretender, he was Lieutenant General of the Austrian Army from 1733 and Emperor Don Carlos VI, as King of Naples, granted him the title of Count of Vinyals-Veguer, by Decree given at Vienna, 5 April 1732.
1 CONT 
1 CONT José de Vinyals y de Veguer, a native of Barcelona, obtained the privilege of Noble of the Principality of Catalonia, in Barcelona, on April 2, 1708.
1 CONT 
1 CONT John and Matthew of Vinyals and Ribot and the son of the latter, Savior of Vinyals and Ciurana, neighbors of Foixá, were qualified as knights in the Cortes of 1626.
1 CONT 
1 CONT José Vinials de la Torre Guitart, born in Sarriá (Catalonia), proved his nobility to exercise the office of Nuncio to the Holy Office of the Inquisition of Barcelona, in 1660, with his wife Maria Escarrer and Oliver, born in L'Hospitalet.
1 CONT 
1 CONT José Viñals y Veguer, obtained memorial on privilege of Caballero, in 1785, and Antonio Viñals, made file on privilege of nobility, in 1815, refusing it.
1 CONT 
1 CONT José Viñales, a resident of Ponferrada (León), tried its nobility before the Sala de los Hijosdalgo of the Royal Chancery of Valladolid, in 1791.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Source: https://heraldicahispana.com/npds/static.php?op=aaappp.php&var=Vinyals%2002
