0 @N14006@ NOTE === Eldest son of Hugh IV ov Cyprus. Suceede ===
1 CONT Eldest son of Hugh IV ov Cyprus. Suceeded to the throne in 1359-1369.  King durring the black death of 1347-8. Peter began by taking over the port of Korykos from its Armenian inhabitants and then in 1362 he travelled to the West and toured Europe
1 CONC , recruting men for a crusade.  He and his army left Venice in 1365 and rendeZvousing with the Cypriot forces ad Rhodes, decended on the Egyptian city of Alexanderia.  The garrison was taken completely unawares; the city was captured and pillaged
1 CONC ; the crusading army then withdrew on learning of the approach of the main Mamluk army from Cairo.  Peter thought that he would be able to retake Jerusalem and the Holy Places of Christendom. He was assassinated by Philip of Ibelin and Henry of Jub
1 CONC ail, and John of Gaurelle.
0 @N14007@ NOTE === !#510-p22; Peter I of Cyprus, Date of ac ===
1 CONT !#510-p22; Peter I of Cyprus, Date of accessin to the throne, 1367/1368; Cousin of Constantine II; Age at time of accession to the throne 29; Length of rule 1 year; Assassinated at age 30; Latin Consort; Assassinated before setting foor in Armenia
1 CONC ; Died 18 Jan 1369; !#552-v3-pt3-T565; !#12109; !#12718-v2-p1157; !1360 King Jerusalem, 1368/69 King Armenia;
